A||||1||kslish||PA Club Website - Suggestions to improve?||||1||
Z||000000||kslish||12-21-2000||07:21 PM||||Hey all,<P>I need suggestions on how to improve the Western PA Fiero Club's website.  It's located at:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.westpennfiero.org</A> <P>I'm sort of out of my own ideas on how to make it better so far (other than clean up the broken links).<P>Don't go too overboard with the ideas.  I'm self-taught at web page creation so my skills are hardly professional.  (Hopefully that will change since I'm going back to school in the spring for computer programming even though I'm a high-school science educator by trade.  Trying to find a teaching job in Pittsburgh, PA is too political and all the money in this town is found in the computer industry anyways.  But, I digress.)  I also try to make sure each page loads quickly for those with dial-up connections. <P>Also, check out the Fiero Infopedia link.  Lots of Fiero info that I have collected over the years is there. <P>Ken S.<BR>Webmaster- Western PA Fiero Club<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||12-21-2000||07:34 PM||||Ken, it looks fine to me!! I am also an autodidactic (self-taught) webmaster -- I turned it into a graphics and design business too........You are mnore than welcome to look at a couple of sites I have done (and would you put links on your site to ours as well?) -- Classic Fiero Owners Group (CFOG) -  <A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A>  and Golden Gate Fieros -  <A HREF="http://www.goldengatefieros.org" TARGET=_blank>www.goldengatefieros.org</A> <P>Keep up the good work, it looks good!!||||reg||1
